{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook, and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after a painful breakup with his girlfriend, erica albright, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and attention from the university administration. mark is then approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who ask him to help them create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees, but soon becomes more interested in creating his own site, which eventually becomes facebook.\n\nas facebook grows in popularity, mark becomes increasingly obsessed with the site, and his relationships with his friends and family begin to suffer. he also becomes embroiled in a series of lawsuits, including one with the winklevoss brothers, who claim that mark stole their idea for facebook.\n\nthe film is directed by david fincher, who is known for his dark and atmospheric style. he does a great job of capturing the mood and tone of the film, and the cinematography is excellent. the script, written by aaron sorkin, is also very good, with witty and engaging dialogue.\n\nthe cast of the film is also excellent, with jesse eisenberg standing out as mark zuckerberg. he brings a lot of depth and nuance to the character, and his performance is very convincing. andrew garfield is also very good as eduardo saverin, mark's friend and business partner. justin timberlake is also good as sean parker, the co-founder of napster, who becomes involved with facebook and helps to take the site to the next level.\n\noveral